cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or reference this specification, please cite it as below."
title: "Royalty OS Trace Layer v3.0"
type: software
version: "0.1.0-candidate"
date-released: "2026-05-27"

authors:
  - family-names: "Shidenkai"
    given-names: "Alpha"
    alias: "SamuraiWriter7"

abstract: >
  Royalty OS Trace Layer v3.0 is a machine-readable specification
  for recording authorized AI usage, retrieval events, provenance signals,
  attribution evidence, and allocation-trigger candidates. It defines
  trace events, allocation triggers, outlier origin detection, privacy-aware
  evidence handling, and the separation between trace, review, and allocation
  in AI-era value circulation infrastructure.

keywords:
  - royalty-os
  - trace-layer
  - ai-attribution
  - ai-provenance
  - rag
  - c2pa
  - watermarking
  - allocation-trigger
  - outlier-origin-detection
  - value-circulation
  - ai-governance
  - machine-readable-permission
  - creator-economy
  - provenance
  - traceability

repository-code: "https://github.com/SamuraiWriter7/royalty-os-trace-layer-v3.0"

